        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Two rules of thumb for beginning sentences are (1) get to the subject quickly and (2) get to the verb and object quickly (see pp. 127–130). Go through a page of your writing and underline the first seven or eight words of every sentence. Revise those in which you do not come to the subject and the verb in those opening words.",
            "block_bbox": [
                127,
                184,
                784,
                279
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
